f 1074 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X] & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{9}{2}.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+36\\cdot \\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X] & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436001 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436001 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109064" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436001 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436001 #edb/ref 1071 "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=3,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[7X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436001 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eff26da6-299d-5b1f-93b8-02b4dbf809cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436001 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X] & ={7}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =49\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=3.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}+4\\cdot \\frac{2}{7}+16\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{7}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X] & =49\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =49\\cdot \\frac{10}{7} \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436002 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436002 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129394" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436002 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436002 #edb/ref 1071 "If $\\text{Var}[X]=100,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[3-0.2X].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f691affc-d374-513b-ace4-47b0fed08cd8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436002 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-0.2$ and $b=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3-0.2X] & ={(-0.2)}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =0.04\\cdot 100 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436003 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436003 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "08e8ef20-2a38-5e05-81d